jobs.description:
As a Production Employee at Bavaria in Lieshout, you will play an important role in brewing and packaging one of the Netherlands' most iconic beers. In our state-of-the-art bottling facility, you help fill approximately 100,000 cans and bottles every hour.

Working at Bavaria means being involved in the entire production process. Together with your colleagues, you ensure that production runs as smoothly and efficiently as possible. Your shift starts and ends with a handover, where you discuss production results, breakdowns, and other important details with operators from the other teams.

At Bavaria, you will enjoy a varied role with responsibilities including:

- Setting up and adjusting machines;
- Troubleshooting common technical issues;
- Performing maintenance on the production line;
- Sorting returnable bottles;
- Supplying packaging machines with caps and rolls;
- Monitoring and checking beer quality.

Working Hours & Availability

Until January, you will work in a fixed 3-shift rotation with a repeating three-week cycle:

- Week 1: 4 to 5 night shifts from 10:00 PM to 06:00 AM
- Week 2: 3 afternoon shifts from 02:00 PM to 10:00 PM and 2 morning shifts from 06:00 AM to 02:00 PM
- Week 3: 3 morning shifts from 06:00 AM to 02:00 PM and 2 afternoon shifts from 02:00 PM to 10:00 PM

From January onwards, you will transition to a fixed 5-shift rotation schedule:

- 2 early shifts from 06:00 AM to 02:00 PM
- 2 late shifts from 02:00 PM to 10:00 PM
- 2 night shifts from 10:00 PM to 06:00 AM
- 4 days off

Are you ready to become part of this dynamic family-owned company? Apply now and you could soon be working in the bottling facility of Royal Swinkels!

- You are available to work in a 5-shift rotation schedule and till januari in a 3-shift schedule; 
- You have a good command of either the Dutch or English language;
- You are eager to learn and develop new skills.

SamenvattingDo you enjoy being active and like the idea of ​​being part of DHL? Then be sure to read on and discover what this job has to offer. Good work! Over de functieThis role is ideal if you enjoy being active and like variety.
Your responsibilities:
- Sorting and scanning parcels;
- Loading and unloading shipments;
- Working on the conveyor belt;
- Handling parcels of various sizes and weights;
- Supporting efficient daily warehouse operations.

The warehouse worker position involves working in a two-shift system. The working hours are 15:00/17:00-23:00, 17:00-02:30, 23:00-07:00. It is a job for 24–32 hours per week. 
Over het bedrijfYour new employer, DHL, is an essential link in the global logistics process. Packages are sorted, shipped, and delivered in more than 200 countries. You will be working at the Amsterdam location. You will work in a modern environment and be part of a driven and motivated team. 
Wat wij vragenYou have your own accomodation in the Netherlands; 
Good command of the Dutch or English language;
Performing physical work is no problem for you;
You are motivated, work well in a team, and are accurate;
You are available to work flexibly in a two-shift system.

Of course, these points are essential for the role of order picker, but we are primarily interested in who you are! Inspire us.

Wat wij biedenA salary of €14,99 gross per hour;
Shift allowance:125% → from 20:00 to 24:00
130% → from 00:00 to 07:00;

Weekend allowance:+50% on Saturdays
+100% on Sundays

Travel allowance up to €13,80 per day;
Extra money when you work overtime: 150%.

Meer informatieApplying only takes 2 minutes. Do you have any questions? Kamila will be happy to anwser them on:+31625477379 or k.spiewak@carriere.com Good work!

SamenvattingStart as an Orderpicker in Woerden and help keep Jumbo stores stocked across the Netherlands. Earn up to €23.39 gross per hour, and enjoy a hands-on logistics job with clear routines and a supportive team. No specific education required, just motivation and a willingness to learn. Good work!Over de functieAs an Orderpicker, you’ll prepare orders for Jumbo stores across the Netherlands using a modern voice-pick system. Depending on the assignment, you will work in a warm (+18°C) or chilled (+2°C to +4°C) area at the warehouse.

Your tasks:
-  Picking orders with a voice-pick system;
-  Placing products on trolleys or pallets;
-  Checking orders for accuracy and quality;
-  Keeping your workspace clean and organized;
-  Following warehouse and safety procedures;

This job is for 32–40 hours per week in a two-shift system, with occasional weekend work.
The worktimes are from 06.00 - 14:00 and 14.00 - 21:00.
Over het bedrijfAt Jumbo’s distribution centre in Woerden, teamwork keeps things moving. Every day, colleagues work together to prepare orders and make sure stores across the Netherlands receive the groceries and everyday products their customers need. You will join a modern, well-organized workplace where everyone plays a part. Clear procedures, a focus on quality and helpful colleagues make it a great place to gain experience in logistics and develop your skills.
Wat wij vragen- Own accommodation in The Netherlands. For this job we don't provide housing;
- Basic English skills to understand instructions and communicate with your team
- Willingness to work in warm and chilled areas;
- Physically stable and comfortable with walking and lifting during the shift;
- You are available to work in 2-shifts.

Of course, these points are essential for the role of order picker, but we are primarily interested in who you are! Inspire us.
Wat wij bieden- A salary between €14.99 and €15.21 gross per hour for work in the warm warehouse and €15.37–€15.59

As a Logistics Employee, you will start your journey in the Value Added Services (VAS) department. Together with your team, you will make sure products are processed accurately, packed properly and prepared for shipment to customers around the world.

- Inspect incoming goods;
- Load and unload containers;
- Label and repack products when needed;
- Pick, check and prepare customer orders for shipment;
- Work closely with your colleagues to ensure everything runs smoothly.

After approximately two months, you will move to another logistics department. Here, you will learn new tasks and gain even more variety in your work. This gives you the opportunity to develop yourself into an all-round logistics employeeDo you see yourself working in a dynamic logistics environment where you can develop your skills and grow within the company? Don’t wait any longer and apply today! We will contact you as soon as possible to discuss the opportunities.

Because you will also be working with an electric pallet truck (EPT) in this position, if you do not have any prior experience with it, you will be required to complete a training course and obtain the corresponding certificate.

- You speak and understand English well;
- You are available to work full-time;
- You are willing to work in a two-shift schedule after your training period;
- You have experience working in logistics or production;
- You are motivated and enjoy working hands-on.
- Holds an EPT certificate or is willing to obtain one through Olympia.
